TEXT 64 -376 Left 3 ;#118 Series PIN diode RF switch
TEXT 64 -312 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XpYsCM_Wf50
TEXT 64 -264 Left 2 ;The DC bias current through the PIN diode sets its RF resistance, so the supply voltage controls how much of the 10 MHz signal reaches the 50 ohm scope input.
TEXT 64 256 Left 2 !.model DPIN D(Is=5e-12 N=2 Rs=1 Cjo=1p Tt=1u Bv=200)
TEXT 64 304 Left 2 !.step param VS list 0.95 4.52 8.2
TEXT 64 352 Left 2 !.tran 0 2.4u 2u 0.2n
TEXT 64 568 Left 2 ;Alan's series SPST fixture at 7:00: a 10 MHz 5 Vpp sine from a 50 ohm\ngenerator, 0.1u coupling capacitors, a 1k bias feed bypassed by 0.47u,\na 680 ohm DC return, and a 50 ohm terminated scope input.
TEXT 64 712 Left 2 ;DPIN is an illustrative PIN diode model. Alan does not name the part, and\nno manufacturer PIN model is held in this collection. Tt=1u is the carrier\nlifetime that keeps charge stored in the intrinsic region across an RF\ncycle, which is what makes the diode act as a resistor set by the DC bias\ncurrent instead of rectifying the signal.
TEXT 1000 256 Left 2 !.meas tran IBIAS AVG I(Dpin) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 1000 304 Left 2 !.meas tran VSCOPE_PP PP V(SCOPE) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 1000 352 Left 2 !.meas tran VD_PP PP V(ANODE,CATHODE) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 1000 400 Left 2 !.meas tran ID_PP PP I(Dpin) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 1000 448 Left 2 !.meas tran RD PARAM VD_PP/ID_PP
